# Trayscale (unofficial Tailscale GUI, v0.19.0 flathub) — its manifest only
# grants filesystems=/run/tailscale:ro, and it never sets the settable
# Socket field on tailscale.com/client/local.Client (checked its own
# source: app.go, ui.go, settings.go, preferences.go — no match for
# "Socket"; confirmed the upstream client and safesocket packages read no
# env var either). No override exists anywhere in the chain — the fixed
# path is the only way in.
app       dev.deedles.Trayscale
expects   /run/tailscale/tailscaled.sock — hardcoded, no env/flag/pref override (verified against upstream source, see note above)
daemon    tailscaled --tun=userspace-networking --socket=/run/user/$(id -u)/tailscale/tailscaled.sock --statedir=~/.local/state/tailscale
bridge    /run/tailscale=/run/user/$(id -u)/tailscale
verify    killed every running Trayscale instance first (GApplication is single-instance and would otherwise just D-Bus-activate the old, unbridged process); then flatpak/bridge.sh dev.deedles.Trayscale /run/tailscale=/run/user/1001/tailscale — log went from "dial unix .../tailscaled.sock: no such file or directory" to real daemon responses: "500 Internal Server Error: Taildrop disabled; no storage directory" and "not connected to the tailnet" — both are the daemon answering, not a connection failure
status    verified
note      tray icon itself does not register on this host — separate, pre-existing gap: "register StatusNotifierItem ... was not provided by any .service files" (Phosh's panel doesn't run a StatusNotifierWatcher). Unrelated to this bridge; the app window and daemon connectivity both work.
note      binaries came from tools/deb2home.sh --no-deps tailscale (Debian's tailscale .deb has no route through the normal apt path — check-package.sh calls it UNLIKELY, postinst calls systemctl; deb2home skips maintainer scripts entirely, which is exactly right here since we run tailscaled by hand anyway)
